0..79 Comment "//! An atom named inside the abstraction that binds it, read by its depth below"
80..95 Comment "//! its binder."
96..99 Comment "//!"
100..176 Comment "//! Admission re-mints an atom with its binder, so a rule naming the channel"
177..254 Comment "//! its restriction abstracts is one rule whatever the atom is called. A rule"
255..332 Comment "//! stating a freshness condition fires only where its instance names no atom"
333..348 Comment "//! it may not."
349..352 Comment "//!"
353..432 Comment "//! Matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s replay count the abstractions"
433..511 Comment "//! between an occurrence and its binder. A rule\'s variable is a hole over the"
512..589 Comment "//! atoms it may name, so the check decides an overlap under the condition it"
590..660 Comment "//! composes. Each theory below normalizes one process its rules meet."
661..664 Comment "//!"
665..727 Comment "//! - owes: #1934 — a rule matching a variable both under an"
728..759 Comment "//!   abstraction and beside it"
760..835 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr` — that rule, refused"
836..889 Comment "//! - cites: [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting], § 2"
890..966 Comment "//! - cites: [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science], § 4"
967..1026 Comment "//! - cites: [Milner-1999-communicating_and_mobile_systems]"
1027..1101 Comment "//! - cites: [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]"
1102..1181 Comment "//! - cites: [Miller-1991-a_logic_programming_language_with_lambda_abstraction]"
1182..1185 Comment "//!"
1186..1309 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2006.12.002 \"Fernández and Gabbay, Nominal rewriting\""
1310..1475 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]: https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139084673 \"Pitts, Nominal Sets: Names and Symmetry in Computer Science\""
1476..1628 Comment "//! [Milner-1999-communicating_and_mobile_systems]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7950513W \"Milner, Communicating and Mobile Systems: the π-Calculus\""
1629..1810 Comment "//! [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]: https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-3975(97)00143-6 \"Mayr and Nipkow, Higher-order rewrite systems and their confluence\""
1811..2028 Comment "//! [Miller-1991-a_logic_programming_language_with_lambda_abstraction]: https://doi.org/10.1093/logcom/1.4.497 \"Miller, A Logic Programming Language with Lambda-Abstraction, Function Variables, and Simple Unification\""
2030..2106 Comment "/// A send on a restricted channel, which no process outside the restriction"
2107..2184 Comment "/// can receive: the process never moves, so it is the inert one. The checker"
